EastSun (with D:\HT9045\system\Mot_Table.csv open): "你外掛軟體可以包含開啟CSV時可以
向excel有表格可以編輯嗎?"
- a custom text editor for *.csv (priority default; 以文字開啟 in its bar, a
  table icon on a .csv text editor and 以表格開啟 in the explorer to go back)
- media/csv.js: click / type / F2 / double-click edits, Enter / Tab / arrows
  / Home / End / PageUp / PageDown move, Esc cancels, Shift+arrows or a drag
  select a block, Delete clears it, Ctrl+C / Ctrl+X / Ctrl+V tab separated
  (to and from Excel), insert / delete rows, find (Ctrl+F, Enter / F3), the
  first row frozen as the header (guessed, can be turned off), column
  widths by dragging. Only the rows in sight are drawn (5003 rows: 42).
- lib/csvtable.js: parse with the offset of every field; a change replaces
  ONLY the text of the cells it changes (quoted stays quoted, a comma /
  quote / line break gets quotes, cells past a row's end / rows past the
  last get the separators and the file's line end) -- the machine's
  settings are CSV, the file is never re-written. Every change is one
  WorkspaceEdit in VS Code's document: Ctrl+S saves, Ctrl+Z undoes (VS
  Code's own). The offsets are read again right before each edit (two
  quick edits in a row land right).
- a file VS Code decoded wrong (Big5 read as UTF-8: U+FFFD, the bytes not
  UTF-8) is read only and says how to reopen it as Big5 -- saving would
  destroy those characters (Language.csv, AUOTMOTIVE.CSV on this machine).
Also: the Tab-order view no longer counts a control hidden when the page runs
(shown only while designing since 0.64) as a Tab stop -- it is none then.

Tests (all 4 layers pass): lib (parse / edits / rows / clipboard / Big5,
and the real Mot_Table.csv read in memory: one value changed = only those
bytes, changed back = the same file), probe (the table in headless Edge:
5003 rows 42 drawn, type + Enter = one edit, block copy, Delete = one edit,
paste, Esc, find, read only), smoke (the edits written into the document,
two in a row, paste, insert / delete, copy, a Big5 file refused), real VS
Code (a COPY of Mot_Table.csv: one cell = only its bytes, not saved, VS
Code's undo takes it back exactly).

